+# Answer: a memory write no longer evicts the static system prompt
+
+## Cause
+
+`build_system()` returned the whole system prompt as one text block with a single
+`cache_control` marker at the end. Caching is prefix-based, so any byte change
+after the start of the block is a cache miss for everything. `save_fact` appends to
+`athlete.facts`, which is rendered inside that block, so each save changed the
+prefix and re-cached the ~1000-token instructions along with the facts. That
+matches `NOTES.md` and the `usage.jsonl` pattern: `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and
+`cache_creation_input_tokens` near the full prompt size on the call right after a save.
+
+## Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`)
+
+The system prompt is now two text blocks, each with `cache_control: ephemeral`:
+
+1. `INSTRUCTIONS`: a constant, byte-stable across users and days.
+2. `athlete_context(a, today)`: the per-athlete tail (date, name, zones, goal,
+   facts, language).
+
+A `save_fact` now invalidates only block 2. Block 1 stays in cache.
+
+Nothing else changed. Tools are still selected per message and placed above the
+system prompt, so a message that adds a tool group still misses the cache once.
+Fact selection is still "include all facts", as before.
+
+## Checked offline
+
+Stubbed `build_request` for two athletes on two days, with a fact added in between:
+
+- The instructions block is byte-identical in all three requests.
+- The tail changes after `save_fact`.
+- There are exactly two `cache_control` markers, which is within the limit of 4.
+
+I did not call the API. There is no `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY` in this environment, and I
+did not deploy anything.
+
+## Open risk: the minimum cacheable length
+
+Anthropic only caches a prefix that is at least the model's minimum length
+(1024 tokens for Sonnet-class models). Here the first marker's prefix is the core
+tools plus `INSTRUCTIONS`. `INSTRUCTIONS` is about 2,480 characters, and the core
+tools are about 420 characters. From the existing `usage.jsonl` numbers, that prefix
+is probably just under 1024 tokens. If it is, the first marker is silently ignored,
+the only effective marker is the tail one, and the bug is back: a memory write
+re-caches everything.
+
+I could not confirm this without an API call. To check:
+
+- After deploying, send a message and then a `save_fact` message within 5 minutes.
+  Then look at the next call in `logs/usage.jsonl`. If `cache_creation_input_tokens`
+  is roughly the tail size (~100-300 tokens), the fix works. If it is roughly the full
+  prompt (~1000+), the static block is below the minimum.
+- Or use the token-counting endpoint on the static prefix.
+
+If it is below the minimum, the options are to lengthen the static block (only with
+useful content, not filler) or to move a stable part of the per-athlete data into
+the static block. I did not pad the prompt, because that would add tokens on every
+cache write without improving the answer.
+
+## Verify with the usage log
+
+- Two messages within 5 minutes: the second call's `cache_read_input_tokens` should
+  cover roughly the whole prompt.
+- After a `save_fact`: the next call's `cache_read_input_tokens` should be about the
+  static block, and `cache_creation_input_tokens` about the tail only.
